From ca802186f125ab6d3cbac7f38617f0c14e443459 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:50:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): inferred park awaiting is judged by its wake
 mechanism; trackers don't re-wake for a handled status [daveey]

Review fixes for owner wake / visible waits:
- kanban_wait_info.describe: main's "no producer, no park" records an inferred awaiting on every park
  ({kind: clock, inferred} for a plain schedule/continuation). An inferred clock/external guess now falls through to
  the wake_check / wake_at logic (a continuation checkpoint is a clock wait, not "no producer"); a declared clock
  window is a live producer; awaiting.gateway is in the label and the premise.
- wait-check: implicit --from. Run as a dispatcher probe (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK/HERMES_KANBAN_DB), a task check is not
  met while the target still sits in the status the waiter's last condition_met already reported, so a tracker
  re-parked after handling review/triage/parked-agent waits for the next change instead of waking every interval.
- parked_waits: a failed remote read skips remote cards (logged) instead of dropping the whole owner-wake tick.
- remote stalled counts use the same status test as parked (a legacy unknown row is never stalled).
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_session_activity.py     | 14 ++++-
 hermes_cli/kanban_wait_check.py           | 33 +++++++++++
 hermes_cli/kanban_wait_info.py            | 35 +++++++++---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_wait_info.py | 69 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 140 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

